# Skill authoring

## SKILL.md frontmatter

Required: `name`, `description`. Audit skills default to `scope: project`.

```yaml
---
name: my-audit-skill
description: >-
  Third-person description with WHAT and WHEN (trigger phrases).
  Use when the user asks for …
scope: project
---
```

`description` is used for agent discovery — include Russian trigger phrases when relevant.

## Folder layout

```
skills/<name>/
├── SKILL.md
├── scripts/       # node *.mjs helpers; run from target repo cwd
├── assets/        # JSON checklists, markers — edit here, not in target repo
└── references/    # optional long-form docs
```

Scripts and assets live **inside the skill folder**, never in the target project.

## SKILL.md body structure

1. **Purpose** — one paragraph
2. **Skill layout** — show `<SKILL_DIR>/` tree
3. **Quick start** — copy-pasteable `node <SKILL_DIR>/scripts/….mjs`
4. **Workflow** — checkbox checklist
5. **Agent instructions** — explicit steps for the agent (resolve SKILL_DIR, run script, read profile)

Reference `.audit/profile.json` fields when the skill depends on `audit-init`. Report outputs go to `.audit/reports/*.json` — see `audit-artifacts.mdc`. Every artifact must include `generatedBy` from `skills/_shared/generated-by.mjs`.

## Agents (`agents/*.md`)

Optional YAML frontmatter: `name`, `description`, `scope`. Body defines a strict read-only contract and structured report format (🔴/🟡/🟢), similar to migration verifiers.
